    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0047" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/11–1044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Near Eastern
                        and African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stettinius</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-11-23">November 23, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Stettinius</hi>: As you may perhaps have noticed
                    from airgram no. 74 of November 10 from our Minister at Jidda, King Ibn Saud
                    “consented readily” to permit the survey of a possible pipe-line route to the
                        Mediterranean<anchor n="42" xml:id="d25-f1"/> by the Arabian American Oil
                    Company during a visit of officials of that company to Riyadh last month.</p>
                <pb facs="0048" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/>
                <p>This is good news and a further indication that the King is disposed to play ball
                    with us in everything that pertains to the development of our great oil
                    concession in his country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d25-f1" n="42" xml:id="d25-f1-content">
                <p>In a memorandum of November 25 in reply the Under Secretary of State said that he
                    had noted favorably the King’s consent to permit a survey of a possible
                    pipe-line route across Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
